vices business with a $789M market cap on $258M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +5.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -451% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $6M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 2.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 25% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 81% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8074645148853375},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Communication Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 36% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 241% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Nextdoor (NXDR) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/05/nextdoor-nxdr-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/?source=iedfolrf0000001","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793909462.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Nextdoor expects Q4 revenue of $78M-$80M with adjusted EBITDA of $10M-$11M as WAU growth flattens seasonally (NASDAQ:NXDR)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667133-nextdoor-expects-q4-revenue-of-78m-80m-with-adjusted-ebitda-of-10m-11m-as-wau-growth-flattens","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793909227.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Nextdoor Holdings, Inc. (NXDR) Reports Break-Even Earnings for Q3","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024679/nextdoor-holdings-inc-nxdr-reports-break-even-earnings-for-q3?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3024679","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793896202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earni